---
const briefTemplate = `AI RESEARCH-TO-DECISION BRIEF

Decision question
[What exactly needs a decision? Include the deadline and decision owner.]

Evaluation criteria
1. [Criterion] — [Why it matters] — [Weight: high / medium / low]
2. [Criterion] — [Why it matters] — [Weight: high / medium / low]
3. [Criterion] — [Why it matters] — [Weight: high / medium / low]

Evidence map
• Primary sources: [official documentation, original data, direct statements]
• Supporting sources: [credible analysis, specialist reporting]
• Signals: [reviews, community discussion, early indicators]
• Evidence gaps: [what you could not verify]

Facts
• [Verified claim] — [source link] — [date checked]

Inferences
• [What the evidence suggests] — [reasoning]

Uncertainties
• [What remains unknown] — [how it could change the decision]

Recommendation
[The action you recommend, for whom, and why now.]

Risks and mitigations
• [Risk] — [likelihood / impact] — [mitigation or trigger to stop]

Next action
[Named owner] will [specific action] by [date].

Review date
[Date to revisit this brief, plus what new evidence should be checked.]`;
---

<section class="brief-system" aria-labelledby="brief-system-title">
  <div class="brief-intro">
    <span class="section-tag">Template asset / 001</span>
    <h2 id="brief-system-title">AI research-to-decision brief</h2>
    <p>A one-page working document for decisions that need evidence, judgment and a clear next move.</p>
  </div>

  <ol class="brief-steps" aria-label="How to use this template">
    <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Frame the decision</strong><p>Write one decision question before opening more tabs. Name the owner and the deadline.</p></div></li>
    <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Collect with a source hierarchy</strong><p>Start with primary sources, then add supporting analysis. Keep the link beside every important claim.</p></div></li>
    <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Let AI organize, then verify</strong><p>Use AI to extract claims, compare options and spot gaps. Verify the claims that would change your recommendation.</p></div></li>
    <li><span>04</span><div><strong>Commit to the brief</strong><p>Separate facts from inferences, state the uncertainty, choose a next action and schedule the review date.</p></div></li>
  </ol>

  <div class="brief-copy-area">
    <div class="brief-copy-head">
      <div>
        <span class="section-tag">Copy and use</span>
        <p>Paste this into Notion, Google Docs, your project tracker or an AI chat.</p>
      </div>
      <button class="copy-brief" type="button" data-copy-brief>Copy template</button>
    </div>
    <textarea class="brief-template" readonly aria-label="AI Research-to-Decision Brief template">{briefTemplate}</textarea>
  </div>

  <p class="brief-note">Useful rule: if a claim would materially change the decision, attach its original source and label its confidence.</p>
</section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-copy-brief]").forEach((button) => {
    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const template = button.closest(".brief-copy-area")?.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>(".brief-template");
      if (!template) return;

      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(template.value);
        button.textContent = "Copied";
        window.setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = "Copy template"; }, 1800);
      } catch {
        template.focus();
        template.select();
        button.textContent = "Select to copy";
      }
    });
  });
</script>
